Manual checklist Group 3 (relay/valve), firmware v2.1.0
Session: miniterm COM3 115200, 2026-10-14
Full raw console capture provided by the tester.

Confirmed PASS:
- relay on/off/toggle/toggle: correct OPEN/CLOSED transitions; repeated 'relay on' -> W601 already on.
- relay pulse 1000: [VALVE] OPEN (pulse) -> CLOSED (pulse end); tick delta ~1030 ms, matches the 1 s pulse.
- relay pulse (no ms arg) -> E603 pulse must be 100-10000 ms.
- relay pulse 1000 while relay already ON -> E604 relay is already on - pulse not possible (RL-3, expected).
- relay schedule 3 3: multiple ON/OFF cycles at ~3000-3030 ms each; 'relay schedule off' stops the cycle;
  second 'relay schedule off' -> W605 schedule is not running.
- relay pulse 10000 interrupted by 'logout': valve was mid-pulse (OPEN) when 'logout' ran; log shows
  [VALVE] CLOSED (logout) immediately - matches RL-7 (logout stops pulse/schedule, forces relay off).
- distance alarm 30\ (stray backslash typo) -> correctly rejected: E708 alarm must be 5-300 cm or 'off'
  (bonus NFR-4 confirmation: malformed input handled gracefully).

Findings needing follow-up (not yet confirmed as firmware bugs):

1. DIODE POLARITY (TC-RL-01): tester reports the GPIO4 indicator diode lights when the relay is OFF and is
   dark when ON - the opposite of RL-1a ("Діод світить, коли реле увімкнене"). Could be firmware (GPIO4
   driven active-low) or a wiring mistake (diode cathode connected to 3V3 instead of GND, or reversed
   polarity) on this specific physical build. Asked the tester to verify the physical wiring against the
   schematic (GPIO4 -> resistor -> anode -> cathode -> GND) before this is filed as a firmware bug.

2. RELAY AUTO-ON TRIGGER (TC-RL-13): the valve was already left OPEN (from an earlier 'relay schedule off'
   stopped mid-ON-phase) before 'relay auto on' was exercised, so the whole auto-trigger sequence in this
   log cannot show a CLOSED->OPEN transition - it is inconclusive, not a confirmed defect. A clean re-test
   was proposed: explicitly close the relay first, confirm via 'relay status', then re-test the 'distance
   alarm <n>' + 'relay auto on' + near/far 'distance' sequence from a known closed state.

Follow-up (clean re-test, tester confirmed):
  relay off -> W601 relay already off
  relay status -> [VALVE] closed, auto off, cycles 220
  distance alarm 25 -> [SONAR] alarm at 25 cm
  relay auto on -> [VALVE] auto on - valve opens on sonar proximity alarm
  distance -> echo 24.1 cm; PROXIMITY ALARM (threshold 25 cm); [VALVE] OPEN (distance alarm) - SAME response
  relay status -> [VALVE] OPEN, auto on, cycles 222
Confirms RL-5 works correctly: the valve opens automatically the moment a measurement crosses the alarm
threshold, no separate 'relay on' needed. TC-RL-13 = PASS, finding #2 withdrawn (was inconclusive test, not
a bug). Side note: cycles went 220 -> 222 for a single OFF->ON switch, consistent with the already-known
BUG-005 (cycles +2 per switch) still present on 2.1.0 - not a new finding.

Diode polarity (finding #1): tester confirmed physical wiring matches the schematic (GPIO4 -> resistor ->
anode -> cathode -> GND). Later found to be a wiring error (diode was not connected per fw_7/WIRING.md); after rewiring the diode behaves correctly. Not a firmware defect.
